    cout: 400,
    composition: "1 Constantin Valdor",
    notes:
      "Captain-General of the Legio Custodes, the Emperor's Shield, Magisterium Ultima. Constantin Valdor stands at the right hand of the Emperor, whose most faithful companion he is, watching over him with unwavering devotion and martial prowess all but unequalled. The latter, combined with Valdor's physical and mental abilities, has led him to be described in hushed tones at the Imperial Court as the \"unacknowledged Primarch\". It is a fallacious claim, for however mighty he may be, Valdor plays a less ambitious role, that of Lord Commander of the Custodian Guard. To Valdor, glory and conquest, dominion and victory, are but petty childishness compared to the duty he has sworn to fulfil. Thus, although Constantin Valdor's rank places him in some respects above even the Primarchs, and he is at the heart of Imperial power on Terra, he rarely exercises his influence, save in matters that concern him directly, and never in the service of any personal ambition whatsoever. But should his role be called into question, or worse, should the Emperor or His representatives be threatened, Valdor would become a demigod of vengeance: invincible and relentless.",
